# Citation File Format. GitHub renders this as a "Cite this repository"
# button on the repo page. Zenodo and many citation managers also read it.
# See https://citation-file-format.github.io for spec.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this data warehouse, software, or visualization platform in academic work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "exoplanet_citation: a public citation-graph warehouse and 3D visualization platform for confirmed exoplanets"
abstract: >-
  A daily-refreshed open-source data warehouse linking the NASA Exoplanet
  Archive's confirmed exoplanets to the scientific papers that announced
  them. Citation coverage at 99.89% via a four-tier resolver (NASA ADS
  bibcode, arXiv API, ADS title search, manual triage). Includes Gaia DR3
  host-star enrichment, a FastAPI service over the warehouse, and a React +
  Three.js + WebXR frontend with a per-vantage starfield rasterizer that
  reprojects ~1.4M stars from any exoplanet's heliocentric position.
